ghostlight (1.3.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remove built-in localhost, loopback, and link-local restrictions.
    Local HTTP(S) destinations follow ordinary host and capability
    policies (ADR-0155).
  * Include the composed-page behavior and integration repair prepared
    in the unpublished 1.3.3 candidate.

 -- Leonardo Botinelly <hello@sylin.org>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0400

ghostlight (1.3.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Read the composed page across open shadow roots and injected frames,
    extend the same semantics to observation and geometry, and add a
    confirmed repair for foreign MCP client entries (ADR-0151 through
    ADR-0154).

 -- Leonardo Botinelly <hello@sylin.org>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0400

ghostlight (1.3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Demand-start identity follows the runtime override: with
    GHOSTLIGHT_RUNTIME_FILE set, its directory elects the whole
    authority -- discovery, lease, deploy lock, and the demand-started
    sibling -- so a launcher entry can route a development machine at
    its real authority instead of starting a second one (ADR-0150).

 -- Leonardo Botinelly <hello@sylin.org>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0400

ghostlight (1.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Require a deliberate install to adopt another installation's
    browser registration; report owned_elsewhere with the owning
    tree named, and isolate test journeys behind
    GHOSTLIGHT_NATIVE_HOST_DIR (ADR-0149 amendment).

 -- Leonardo Botinelly <hello@sylin.org>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400

